==Battleground==
*1 [[Sir Seal]] spawns after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>.
*1 [[Imperator Sael]] spawns after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>.
*1 [[Zir Zeal]] spawns after 26.67 seconds<sup>800f</sup>.
*1 [[Sir Metal Seal]] spawns as the boss after 33.33 seconds<sup>1,000f</sup>.
*4 [[Sir Seal]]s spawn after 43.33 seconds<sup>1,300f</sup>, delay 46.67~53.33 seconds<sup>1,400f~1,600f</sup>.
*5 [[Imperator Sael]]s spawn after 53.33 seconds<sup>1,600f</sup>, delay 33.33~40 seconds<sup>1,000f~1,200f</sup>.
*3 [[Zir Zeal]]s spawn after 70 seconds<sup>2,100f</sup>, delay 46.67~53.33 seconds<sup>1,400f~1,600f</sup>.
*1 [[Sir Metal Seal]] spawns after 106.67 seconds<sup>3,200f</sup>.
*1 [[Sir Metal Seal]] spawns after 133.33 seconds<sup>4,000f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Sir Seal and Imperator Sael are not anything to worry about; the main threats are Zir Zeal and Sir Metal Seal. Make sure to bring [[:Category:Anti-Metal Cats|anti-Metal]] [[:Category:Crowd-Controller-class Cats|crowd-controllers]] like [[Hoop Cat (Rare Cat)|Hoopmaster Cat]] and some stackable [[:Category:Critical Hit Cats|Critters]] like [[Volley Cat (Rare Cat)|Curry Cat]] and [[Jurassic Cat (Rare Cat)|Catasaurus]] to deal with the Sir Metal Seals, and save [[Ototo Corps#Holy Blast|Holy Blast]] for the Zir Zeals to make their burrowing less dangerous. Any generalist attacker can be used to deal with them, but you can still bring a specialist like [[Ancient Egg: N107 (Rare Cat)|Cat Chief]] to be safe.

==Trivia==
*The many [[Sir Seal|seals]] in Mermaid Lounge may be a reference to the theory that mermaid myths originated from sightings of marine mammals such as manatees, dugongs or seals.
**They might also represent the [[wikipedia:Selkie|selkie]], a mythical creature that can switch between human and seal forms, as selkies are occasionally confused with mermaids.

